Pull and Re-Tag Docker Image on Application Server 1
This README documents the procedure to pull a Docker image on Application Server 1 (stapp01) in the Stratos DC and create a new re-tagged reference as requested by the Nautilus project developers.

Task Objective
Target Server: Application Server 1 (stapp01)

Action 1: Pull the busybox:musl image.

Action 2: Re-tag the image as busybox:media.

Infrastructure Overview
Server Name	Hostname	User	Password	Purpose
Application Server 1	stapp01	tony	Ir0nM@n	Hosts Nautilus Application 1
Jump Host Server	jump-host	thor	mjolnir123	Provides secure access to Stratos DC
Step-by-Step Execution Guide
1. Connect to Application Server 1 via SSH
From the jump host, log in to Application Server 1 using the user credentials:

Bash
ssh tony@stapp01
Provide password: Ir0nM@n when prompted.

2. Pull the Base Image
Download the required busybox:musl image from Docker Hub:

Bash
docker pull busybox:musl
3. Re-Tag the Image
Create a new reference tag named busybox:media pointing to the downloaded image:

Bash
docker tag busybox:musl busybox:media
4. Verify Image Tags
List local Docker images to confirm that both tags exist and share the same image ID:

Bash
docker images
